//? Title: Floyd–Warshall: actual intermediate stages and bounded shortest paths
//? Subtitle: Preserve the original five-vertex matrix and route; distinguish finite, unreachable and negative-cycle-unbounded pairs
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Floyd–Warshall computes a directed cost matrix for every source and destination.
It admits intermediate vertices one at a time, updating distances and first hops
with a compact in-place recurrence. This report preserves the original five-vertex
example, all25 distances and the cost-minus-three route0→4→3→2. Native traces expose
actual stage matrices and strict improvements. A separate negative-cycle control
shows why a global cycle flag does not make every pair unbounded, while validated,
bounded reconstruction prevents malformed next-hop data from causing an endless walk.
)

\toc

> One admitted intermediate can improve a direct route

A graph has vertices0 through n−1 and directed edges carrying finite double costs.
Negative edge weights are allowed. An absent route is represented by positive
infinity, while the zero-length route from a vertex to itself starts at cost zero.
Parallel edges keep the smallest weight; equal-cost candidates retain the existing
first hop. The native API preserves its original matrix layout and strict tie policy.

Start with a three-vertex graph: direct0→2 costs9, while0→1→2 costs2+3=5.
The following method diagram reads that strict improvement from the actual kernel.
Stage0 is the seeded matrix; stage k+1 has completed the sweep admitting vertex k.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_warshall_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace(3,{{0,1,2.},{1,2,3.},{0,2,9.}});
  std::print("| admitted intermediates | D[0][2] | first hop |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto&stage:t.stages)std::print("| {} | {:.0f} | {} |\n",stage.admitted,stage.distance[0][2],stage.next[0][2]);
  const auto&r=t.relaxations.at(0);std::print("\nActual improvement: k {}; pair {} to {}; previous {:.0f}; left {:.0f}; right {:.0f}; candidate {:.0f}; first hop {}.\n",r.k,r.from,r.to,r.previous,r.left,r.right,r.candidate,r.next);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1000);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.circle=true;node.width=1.4;node.height=1.4;node.font_size=27;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke old,chosen;old.color={148,163,184};chosen.color={220,38,38};chosen.width=3;
  d.node("0",{0,0},"0",node).node("1",{4,3},"1",node).node("2",{8,0},"2",node)
   .edge("0","2",std::format("direct {:.0f}",r.previous),old).edge("0","1",std::format("{:.0f}",r.left),chosen).edge("1","2",std::format("{:.0f}",r.right),chosen)
   .text({4,-2},std::format("Admit {}: {:.0f} + {:.0f} = {:.0f}; first hop {}",r.k,r.left,r.right,r.candidate,r.next),26).save_svg("build/floyd_warshall_tiny.svg");
  if(t.relaxations.size()!=1||r.k!=1||r.candidate!=5)throw std::runtime_error("actual intermediate control");
}
```
