> The recurrence and the in-place condition

Let D^(k)[i,j] be the least cost using only intermediates0 through k−1. Initially,
it contains direct edge minima and diagonal zeros. With no relevant negative cycle,
an optimum can be chosen without repeated vertices: removing a nonnegative cycle
cannot make a walk more expensive. Admitting k either keeps the old route or uses
an i-to-k piece followed by a k-to-j piece:

$$
D^{(k+1)}[i,j]=\min\bigl(D^{(k)}[i,j],D^{(k)}[i,k]+D^{(k)}[k,j]\bigr).
$$
\alttext(The next distance is the smaller of the current distance and the route through the newly admitted intermediate vertex.)

The outer loop must control the admitted set. In exact arithmetic without negative
cycles, D[k,k]=0 and the k-th row and column cannot improve during their own sweep,
so the in-place reads give the staged recurrence. This is an existence-of-a-simple-
optimum argument, not a claim that every optimal walk avoids zero-cost cycles.
With negative cycles, raw in-place numbers are retained as execution evidence;
they must not be interpreted as finite shortest costs for affected pairs.

The historical sources are Floyd's
[Algorithm97: Shortest path](https://doi.org/10.1145/367766.368168),CACM5(6),345(1962),
and Warshall's related Boolean reachability result,
[A Theorem on Boolean Matrices](https://doi.org/10.1145/321105.321107),JACM9(1),11–12(1962).
The API here uses positive infinity for absence, finite input weights, strict double
comparisons and explicit next hops; it is not an exact-real arithmetic certificate.

> Preserve the original five-vertex result

The native fixture retains the original nine edges and their order. Its negative
edges create cheaper detours without creating a negative cycle. The entire printed
matrix and route below come from the canonical function. Directed arrows and weight
labels make the original highlighted graph unambiguous.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_warshall_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto edges=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_example_edges();const auto result=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall(5,edges);const auto path=dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(result,0,2);
  std::print("| from / to | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<5;++i){std::print("| {} |",i);for(double cost:result.distance[i])std::print(" {:.0f} |",cost);std::print("\n");}
  std::print("\nOriginal route0 to2: {}; cost {:.0f}; negative-cycle flag {}.\n",path,result.distance[0][2],result.has_negative_cycle);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(80,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.circle=true;node.width=1.3;node.height=1.3;node.font_size=27;
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> position{{0,4},{4,1.3},{2.5,-3.2},{-2.5,-3.2},{-4,1.3}};
  for(std::size_t v=0;v<5;++v)d.node(std::to_string(v),position[v],std::to_string(v),node);
  for(const auto&[u,v,w]:edges){bool selected=false;for(std::size_t k=1;k<path.size();++k)selected|=path[k-1]==u&&path[k]==v;dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;stroke.color=selected?dm::graphics::RGB{220,38,38}:dm::graphics::RGB{148,163,184};stroke.width=selected?3.5:1.7;d.edge(std::to_string(u),std::to_string(v),std::format("{:.0f}",w),stroke);}
  d.text({0,-5.1},"Highlighted0 → 4 → 3 → 2 has cost -4 + 6 - 5 = -3",26).save_svg("build/floyd_warshall_original.svg");
  if(path!=std::vector<std::size_t>{0,4,3,2}||result.distance[0][2]!=-3||result.has_negative_cycle)throw std::runtime_error("original shortest route");
}
