\caption(All25 original distances are preserved. The red directed route0→4→3→2 costs−3, improving on the direct0→2 edge of cost8.)
\alttext(A native five-vertex directed graph prints all nine edge weights. The highlighted route follows the negative-cost edge from zero to four, then four to three and three to two.)

`next[i][j]` stores the first vertex after i on the chosen route. A strict improvement
through k takes the current `next[i][k]`. Repeatedly following first hops for a fixed
destination recovers the route. Cost and hop count are different objectives: the
three-edge detour is cheaper than the one-edge direct route. Equal costs retain
the earlier route; the library does not promise minimum hops or lexicographic paths.

> Actual stage histories expose when an improvement becomes available

The full trace contains the seeded matrix and every post-k matrix, captured during
the same kernel. Each strict improvement records the actual left/right values read,
the replaced cost, the candidate and both old/new first hops. It stores no failed
comparisons as improvements and does not rerun the algorithm to make a history.
The next table and plots query that evidence for the original0-to2 pair.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_warshall_stages.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace(5,dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_example_edges());std::vector<double> stage_x,cost,phase_x,counts;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| admitted | most recent k | D[0][2] | first hop | strict improvements in that sweep |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto&s:t.stages){const auto count=s.admitted?std::count_if(t.relaxations.begin(),t.relaxations.end(),[&](const auto&r){return r.k==s.admitted-1;}):0;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {} | {} |\n",s.admitted,s.admitted?std::to_string(s.admitted-1):"seed",s.distance[0][2],s.next[0][2],count);stage_x.push_back(double(s.admitted));cost.push_back(s.distance[0][2]);labels.push_back(s.admitted?"after"+std::to_string(s.admitted-1):"seed");if(s.admitted){phase_x.push_back(double(s.admitted-1));counts.push_back(double(count));}}
  const auto&w=t.work;std::print("\nOriginal actual work: row guards {}; skipped rows {}; column guards {}; skipped columns {}; finite additions {}; strict sweep improvements {}; final diagonal tests {}.\n",w.row_checks,w.skipped_rows,w.column_checks,w.skipped_columns,w.candidates,w.relaxations,w.diagonal_checks);
  auto history=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();history.lines(stage_x,cost,"Cost",{37,99,235},2).points(stage_x,cost,"",{37,99,235},5).x_tick_labels(labels).title("Actual0-to2 boundary costs").xlab("Seed and completed sweeps").ylab("Raw cost; graph has no negative cycle");
  auto changes=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(counts,{"0","1","2","3","4"}).title("Strict improvements per sweep").xlab("New intermediate k").ylab("Actual improvement records");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(history).add(changes).size(1100,540).title("Complete snapshots and actual strict update records").fit_panels().save_svg("build/floyd_warshall_stages.svg");
}
