> A negative cycle affects particular ordered pairs

A negative cycle makes the cost unbounded below for an i-to-j query exactly when i
can reach a negative-cycle vertex and that vertex can reach j. Repeating the cycle
then lowers the walk cost without limit. The global flag detects existence; it does
not claim every pair can travel through that cycle. Native classification tests
negative diagonals together with the two reachability entries, without rewriting
raw costs to negative infinity or trusting an externally supplied flag alone.

Use a five-vertex control with0→1 cost1,1→2 cost−3,2→1 cost1 and2→3 cost1;
vertex4 is isolated. The cycle1→2→1 costs−2. Sources0,1,2 have unbounded routes
to destinations1,2,3. The diagonal routes0-to0,3-to3 and4-to4 remain finite, while
3-to0 is unreachable. Affected raw matrix entries are diagnostics, not shortest costs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_warshall_negative.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto r=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall(5,{{0,1,1.},{1,2,-3.},{2,1,1.},{2,3,1.}});const auto mask=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_unbounded_pairs(r);std::size_t affected=0;for(const auto&row:mask)affected+=std::count(row.begin(),row.end(),true);
  std::print("| source / destination | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 |\n| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(48,900);dm::graphics::DiagramStroke border;border.color={148,163,184};border.width=.7;
  for(std::size_t j=0;j<5;++j)d.text({1.6*double(j),1.4},std::to_string(j),24);
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<5;++i){d.text({-1.4,-1.6*double(i)},std::to_string(i),24);std::print("| {} |",i);
    for(std::size_t j=0;j<5;++j){const auto status=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_pair_status(r,i,j);const bool bad=status==dm::algorithms::FloydWarshallPairStatus::Unbounded,unreachable=status==dm::algorithms::FloydWarshallPairStatus::Unreachable;const std::string label=bad?"X":unreachable?"U":"F";const auto fill=bad?dm::graphics::RGB{254,202,202}:unreachable?dm::graphics::RGB{255,255,255}:dm::graphics::RGB{191,219,254};const double x=1.6*j,y=-1.6*double(i);
      d.polygon({{x-.7,y-.7},{x+.7,y-.7},{x+.7,y+.7},{x-.7,y+.7}},fill,border).text({x,y},label,25);std::print(" {} |",label);}
    std::print("\n");}
  bool rejected=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(r,0,3);}catch(const std::domain_error&){rejected=true;}
  std::print("\nCycle flag {}; unbounded pairs {}; affected0-to3 path rejected {}.\n",r.has_negative_cycle,affected,rejected);
  std::print("Unaffected4-to4 route {}; unreachable3-to0 route size {}.\n",dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(r,4,4),dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(r,3,0).size());
  std::print("Raw negative-diagonal diagnostics: D[1][1] {:.0f}; D[2][2] {:.0f}.\n",r.distance[1][1],r.distance[2][2]);
  d.text({3.2,3},"Source row → destination column",25).text({3.2,-8.1},"F finite; U unreachable; X unbounded",25).save_svg("build/floyd_warshall_negative.svg");
  if(affected!=9||!rejected)throw std::runtime_error("pair-specific negative-cycle control");
}
