\caption(The nine red X pairs are unbounded through the negative cycle. Finite blue diagonal controls and unreachable white pairs remain distinct despite the global cycle flag.)
\alttext(A native five-by-five status matrix marks rows zero through two and columns one through three as unbounded X; three unaffected diagonal cells are finite F, with the remaining cells unreachable U.)

Pair queries validate complete distance/next shapes and values before examining a
particular pair, so they cost O(n squared) validation plus O(n) querying. The native
whole unbounded-pair mask validates once and uses O(n cubed) worst-case work.
The small display above queries statuses for clarity; it is not a timing benchmark.
In exact arithmetic a negative diagonal certifies a negative cycle. Here the test is
a strict double comparison, so near-zero floating cycles require attention to rounding.

> Guarded work, bounded reconstruction and complete trace admission

The ordinary kernel uses O(n squared+E+n cubed) worst-case work and O(n squared)
owned storage. It skips rows/columns with unreachable operands before addition.
A dense unit-cost graph performs n cubed additions even with no sweep improvements;
a graph with only diagonal reachability performs n additions. Both are actual counts,
not elapsed times. Reuse the native complete-directed-arc generator for the dense
control, with a constant cost attached to each generated arc.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_warshall_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  using Edges=std::vector<std::tuple<std::size_t,std::size_t,double>>;std::vector<double> x,dense_y,empty_y;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| vertices | dense additions | disconnected additions | dense improvements | disconnected skipped rows |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{1u,2u,4u,8u,16u,32u}){Edges edges;for(auto[u,v]:dm::algorithms::complete_directed_graph_edges(n))edges.emplace_back(u,v,1.);const auto a=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_work(n,edges),b=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_work(n,{});
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,a.work.candidates,b.work.candidates,a.work.relaxations,b.work.skipped_rows);x.push_back(double(x.size()));dense_y.push_back(std::log2(double(a.work.candidates)));empty_y.push_back(std::log2(double(b.work.candidates)));labels.push_back(std::to_string(n));}
  auto edges=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_example_edges();const auto bound=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace_entries(5,edges.size());bool quota=false,nonfinite=false,cyclic=false,overflow=false,huge=false;
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace(5,edges,bound-1);}catch(const std::length_error&){quota=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace(2,{{0,1,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()}},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){nonfinite=true;}
  auto malformed=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall(3,{{0,1,1.},{1,2,1.}});malformed.next[0][2]=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(malformed,0,2);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){cyclic=true;}
  const auto max=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();try{dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall(3,{{0,1,max},{1,2,max}});}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace_entries(std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max(),0);}catch(const std::length_error&){huge=true;}
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace(5,edges,bound);const auto first=edges[0];edges[0]={4,4,99.};const bool owned=t.edges[0]==first;
  std::print("\nComplete trace admission: upper entries {}; one below rejected {}; exact bound stages {}; actual improvements {}.\n",bound,quota,t.stages.size(),t.relaxations.size());
  std::print("Checked controls: NaN before quota {}; cyclic external hop chain bounded {}; finite candidate overflow rejected {}; virtual full-width bound rejected {}.\n",nonfinite,cyclic,overflow,huge);
  std::print("Owned graph after caller edit {}; original distance still {:.0f}; empty-graph trace bound {}.\n",owned,t.result.distance[0][2],dm::algorithms::floyd_warshall_trace_entries(0,0));
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,dense_y,"Dense",{220,38,38},2).points(x,dense_y,"",{220,38,38},4).lines(x,empty_y,"Disconnected",{37,99,235},2).points(x,empty_y,"",{37,99,235},4).x_tick_labels(labels).title("Actual additions: dense n cubed versus disconnected n").xlab("Vertex count; consecutive powers of two").ylab("log2 of completed finite additions").legend({"Dense unit costs","Disconnected"},{{220,38,38},{37,99,235}}).size(900,520).save_svg("build/floyd_warshall_controls.svg");
  if(!quota||!nonfinite||!cyclic||!overflow||!huge||!owned)throw std::runtime_error("bounded checked controls");
}
